// The same symptom from the collection scaffold: an OVER-LIMIT
// `array::init` count is bottom on both engines, but the fused loop
// re-minted that bottom FRESH on every quiet cycle.
//
// `SlotFlags::exact_stale` (fusion/emit/scaffold.rs) holds the
// prev-length word when the source is tainted (`recorded =
// select(valid, lenp1, stored)`) but still computed `resized = stored
// != lenp1` against the CLAMPED length — so the held word (0) never
// matched len+1 (1) and every cycle read as a resize, which fires.
// The node-walk's `forced_taint` arm computes no length at all: it
// returns FreshBottom iff the SOURCE triggered, else rides.
//
// The count here is a literal, so it fires only at init:
//   interp: fresh bottom at init, standing bottom after -> the
//           connect's [1] survives -> [1:[i64:1]]
//   jit:    a fresh bottom every cycle re-publishes `v` and clobbers
//           the queued write -> []
//
// The sibling pins in `init-over-limit-aug2026/` cover the clamp's
// other two effects (retained slots, the clobbered length memory).
{
    let v = array::init(16777217, |i: i64| i);
    v <- [1];
    v
}
